# civil-holidays v1
# jurisdiction: IN
# source: Government of India, Ministry of Home Affairs / Dept. of Personnel &
#   Training annual gazette notification of Central Government holidays, tabulated
#   at https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Public_holidays_in_India
# retrieved: 2026-07-21
# categories: public|regional|municipal|religious|school
# notes:
#   Scope is the CENTRAL government gazetted (closed) holiday list; the optional
#   "restricted" holidays are out of scope. The three fixed days (Republic,
#   Independence, Gandhi Jayanti) are the only nationwide statutory holidays.
#   Islamic holidays resolve through islamic_civil (arithmetic); the gazette
#   follows local moon-sighting, so the tabular date can differ by +/-1 day (the
#   observation caveat). Hindu/Buddhist/Sikh/Jain festivals follow regional
#   panchang computations with NO arithmetic rule in the registry: they are
#   encoded as DECREE data — the exact per-year gazette dates for 2023-2026,
#   honestly tabulated, not computed.
# columns: kind | name | args | categories | subdiv | observed
#
# The MHA/DoPT gazette is issued in English and Hindi; the national days carry
# the Hindi (hi) co-official name alongside English (the English primary is the
# join key used by the golds).
# --- national (fixed) ---
fixed         | en:Republic Day ;; hi:गणतंत्र दिवस             | 1 26   | public          |  |
fixed         | en:Independence Day ;; hi:स्वतंत्रता दिवस       | 8 15   | public          |  |
fixed         | en:Mahatma Gandhi's Jayanti ;; hi:महात्मा गांधी जयंती | 10 2   | public          |  |
#
# --- other central gazetted (fixed / computable) ---
fixed         | Christmas                  | 12 25  | public religious |  |
easter        | Good Friday                | -2     | public religious |  |
#
# --- Islamic (islamic_civil; +/-1 observation caveat) ---
calendar_date | Id-ul-Fitr                 | islamic_civil 10 1  | public religious |  |
calendar_date | Id-ul-Zuha (Bakrid)        | islamic_civil 12 10 | public religious |  |
calendar_date | Muharram                   | islamic_civil 1 10  | public religious |  |
calendar_date | Milad-un-Nabi              | islamic_civil 3 12  | public religious |  |
#
# --- Hindu / Buddhist / Sikh / Jain lunisolar (per-year gazette DECREE data) ---
decree        | Holi              | 2023-3-8 2024-3-25 2025-3-14 2026-3-4 2027-3-22    | public religious |  |
decree        | Ram Navami        | 2023-3-30 2024-4-17 2025-4-6 2026-3-26 2027-4-15   | public religious |  |
decree        | Mahavir Jayanti   | 2023-4-4 2024-4-21 2025-4-10 2026-3-31 2027-4-18   | public religious |  |
decree        | Buddha Purnima    | 2023-5-5 2024-5-23 2025-5-12 2026-5-1 2027-5-20    | public religious |  |
decree        | Janmashtami       | 2023-9-7 2024-8-26 2025-8-16 2026-9-4 2027-8-25    | public religious |  |
decree        | Dussehra          | 2023-10-24 2024-10-12 2025-10-2 2026-10-20 2027-10-09 | public religious |  |
decree        | Diwali (Deepavali)| 2023-11-12 2024-10-31 2025-10-20 2026-11-8 2027-10-29 | public religious |  |
decree        | Guru Nanak's Jayanti | 2023-11-27 2024-11-15 2025-11-5 2026-11-24 2027-11-14 | public religious |  |
decree        | Maha Shivaratri   | 2024-3-8 2025-2-26 2026-2-15 2027-3-6             | public religious |  |


